82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (My journey into palliative care began while caring for my mother-in-law during her prolonged illness. That experience taught me that compassionate care is not only about meeting physical needs but also about being present, listening, and offering comfort during life's most difficult moments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (Since then, I have been spending time with elderly people and patients in my community who often have no one to talk to or care for them. Whether it is helping with personal care, providing essential items like food and diapers, or simply sitting beside them and listening to their stories, I have learned that even small acts of kindness can make a meaningful difference.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
